# FigDown — figures as text. Spec: https://github.com/FigDown/figdown

figdown 0.2 flowchart
# The classic learning-bridge / L2 switch forwarding decision (IEEE 802.1D).
# A frame arrives; the switch learns the source, looks up the destination,
# and takes one of three actions. The LOGIC is machine-readable: a reader
# answers "when does a switch flood?" by tracing the Y/N edges — no pixels.
title "L2 Switch Forwarding Decision"

# Semantic classes: the three terminal OUTCOMES. Each label states the
# MEANING; the legend derives from these lines (spec §2.7).
class forward "Forward — send the frame out the single learned egress port" fill=#16a34a
class flood   "Flood — send out every port in the VLAN except the ingress port" fill=#2563eb
class filter  "Filter — discard; destination is out the same port it arrived on" fill=#dc2626

# The wire is external to the decision logic: the frame enters from outside
# the figure (spec §2.8 external — never drawn as a shape, edge ends open).
external wire "from ingress port"

# 0.1 (`FLOWCHART-ROLE-KEYWORDS`): the role is a WORD, not a shape. `process` for the two
# steps, `decision` for the two branch points, `terminator` for the three
# outcomes — the diamond and the rounded ends are DERIVED, and a reading agent
# gets the roles from the model instead of inferring them from geometry.
process learn  "Learn source MAC:\nupdate MAC table\n(SA -> ingress port)"
process lookup "Look up destination MAC\nin MAC table"
decision hit   "Entry found?"
decision same  "Egress port ==\ningress port?"
terminator fwd "Forward out\nlearned port"                    class=forward
terminator fld "Flood to all ports\nin VLAN except ingress"   class=flood
terminator flt "Filter (drop):\nsame-port destination"        class=filter

# top-to-bottom reading order for the decision process.
flow down

flowline wire   -> learn
flowline learn  -> lookup
flowline lookup -> hit
# Miss (unknown unicast, or broadcast/multicast) -> flood.
flowline hit  -[no]->  fld
flowline hit  -[yes]-> same
# Hit, but destination is behind the ingress port -> filter; else forward.
flowline same -[yes]-> flt
flowline same -[no]->  fwd
